# Independent verification of canonical chapter thirteen evidence

Target: 152c7d485aeb7339b0bc8448bef09bca40837a03. No production or manuscript edits. This review checks reproducibility, legacy targets, saved snapshots and the actual claimed tests. Earlier full chapter meaning/authoring review is reused, not re-certified as human approval. The independent path/code review remains ../review-canonical-path-fix/manifest.json, SHA256 bc4363af1354868da3ec4390318d8dcd7024c8baab55ec906c1c34415ea24583.

Root final evidence manifest b5254f61bccaa3c95d775cf517dee11403fe920f8bd4977b53925eb1405488a5 was checked independently: all 98 payloads / 4305382 bytes match declared lengths and SHA256; all 403 identity source entries match actual Git blobs at target commit, including the embedded Doc bootstrap fixtures; current executable matches the saved root hash. The executable hash is not a historical per-command execution attestation. The earlier independent clean build/code overlay and exact generated outputs provide separate reproducibility evidence. Source, aliases and final Markdown match the previously frozen code-review inputs. Two generated Markdown files match commit bytes exactly; both three-file HTML output sets match the independent build's HTML/CSS/manifest bytes. Each output manifest hash resolves to the real saved files. This is an inspectable local snapshot; the compiler need not run to serve its HTML and CSS.

Verification logs: tools 70 passed / 0 failed / 1 ignored; Doc 76 passed / 0 failed; fmt, workspace/all-target Clippy and build commands recorded exit 0. Initial general repository check genuinely failed (missing tracked path, os error 2 before staging the move), retained separately; later check-staged reports 5451 files / 26 tasks / 57 acceptance status entries passed, explicitly no runtime acceptance in that repository check. The root reproduction script writes the generated MD and requires fresh output paths: do not replay it as a read-only checker or reuse an existing output directory. Its failing check run stops before reproduction.json creation; the later saved byte comparison was therefore independently repeated here rather than inferred from that initial exit status.

Initial browser weakness found and preserved: a target merely intersecting the viewport does not demonstrate navigation from elsewhere or final smooth-scroll completion. The root GitHub and initial local records are retained as target existence/URL evidence; the corrected record.txt explicitly narrows them.

Independent public GitHub verification: exact fixed commit URL, HTTP 200, Chromium 151.0.7922.34 via pinned Playwright 1.62.0, 1280x1000, reduced-motion preference. All eight previously reviewed legacy fragments plus seven semantic fragments occur once. The saved GitHub page's embedded rawLines reproduce the exact final Markdown bytes (SHA256 4a689172adad4ef28fc720bfdf85f23600bfcef8cc8b5eaaf1ed3d8ed6d3a4cc). For each of all 15 fragments, the independent probe positions its target outside the viewport at the opposite document end, performs actual hash navigation and waits at least five stable scroll observations. All targets become visible with a changed scroll position. Typical final target top is ~125px; the last limits target at 648.34375px was independently confirmed to be at document scroll end (scrollY == scrollMax == 4679), not unfinished navigation. The eight original GitHub heading URLs are distinct from the seven Doc Section IDs; six explicit aliases plus two unchanged automatic anchors are preserved. This proves behavior on this public fixed GitHub commit, not future GitHub implementation behavior, main-branch cutover or a deployed Pages route. GitHub's own JavaScript was enabled; generated local document HTML remained script-free.

Local corrected navigation: inspected root's strengthened source, then executed that source with only path bindings changed to this independent frozen snapshot and output directory. Three pinned engines x two local non-root prefixes x two widths x seven semantic IDs = 84 real navigations passed. Each starts at the opposite page end and requires changed scrollY equal to target document-top clamped at document end. Source-language ja, eight headings, 674 Ruby nodes, two exact RFC hrefs, loaded CSS, unique IDs and zero scripts were checked. JavaScript was disabled in each local browser context. Screenshots/AX snapshots are saved; representative WebKit 375px and Chromium 1280px opening views were inspected without apparent overlapping annotations in those views. This is not a full-page visual proof or actual screen-reader testing.

Chromium and Firefox Tab traversal passed in eight configurations. Windows Playwright WebKit Tab traversal failed in all four, independently reproduced unchanged. It is explicitly a failure, not a skipped/passed accessibility claim. The separate author's bare-link/platform investigation is outside this reviewer record; no claim about Safari or other WebKit platforms is inferred here.

No remaining blocker found in the corrected bounded evidence. No aggregate T21/J01-J04 completion, deployment, independent release, canonical approval or human review condition is inferred. Original weak checks and the pre-staging failure remain preserved. Root-final source hash records, snapshots and commands make the selected inputs reproducible; network-hosted GitHub behavior is a dated observation. Script path/HEAD inference in the original helpers should be replaced with the saved fixed commit and snapshot paths for replay, as done by github-probe.py and local-probe.py.
